    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, your computer was stuck while downloading Windows updates, which is also why it had pending security patches. We stopped the update services, cleared the corrupted download cache (Windows rebuilds it automatically), repaired the system component store, and verified system file integrity. The update cycle then ran from scratch and completed: all pending updates are now installed, and we confirmed them in the update history. Your computer needed one restart to finish, which is already done. It should now check for updates normally. If a future update gets stuck again, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} and we will apply the same procedure.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Windows Update on {{HOSTNAME}} stuck at download with 0x80-family error at {{TIMESTAMP}}. wuauserv and bits were running, so the client was healthy enough to operate. Remediation sequence: services stopped cleanly, C:\\Windows\\SoftwareDistribution renamed to SoftwareDistribution.old (disposable cache, regenerated on service start), services restarted and detection retriggered from zero. The persistent error required DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth (completed 100%) followed by sfc /scannow (no integrity violations after repair). Full cycle search, download, install and reboot completed. Verification: Get-HotFix lists the pending updates installed same-day; no further download stalls. No in-place repair needed.',
