    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, your computer was failing to join the corporate WiFi and kept asking for credentials. We removed the saved WiFi profile so Windows negotiates the connection from scratch, verified the certificate chain used to validate the network, and synchronized the system clock, which was slightly off and breaking certificate validation. We also confirmed your account was not locked. The computer now connects automatically and stays connected. When you move between floors it may take a few seconds to reassociate, which is normal. If the prompt for credentials returns, reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} without changing anything so we can check the authentication logs.',
