    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, Outlook was freezing and showing errors in some folders, while your mailbox itself was healthy on the web version. We first ruled out add-ins, then ran the built-in repair tool on your local Outlook data file, and when the issue persisted, we rebuilt that file from scratch — it is only a local copy, and all your mail is safely stored on the server, so nothing was lost. Outlook now opens quickly and completes full synchronization. To keep it stable, we recommend archiving old items as we discussed. Please use it normally today and reply to ticket {{TICKET_ID}} if any folder shows errors again.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Outlook client instability on {{HOSTNAME}} at {{TIMESTAMP}}: freezes on open and sync, duplicated items. Mailbox verified healthy in OWA, isolating the fault to the client. Add-ins ruled out via outlook.exe /safe. The local OST (path and size documented with dir) failed SCANPST repair after two passes, so the OST was recreated by renaming the old file (content lives server-side); full resynchronization completed afterwards. A new Outlook profile was not required. Preventive guidance given: archive old items and keep shared folders in online mode. Verification: Outlook opens without freezes, automatic send/receive cycles run, and full sync completes with no "updating folder" hang.',
