    escalation: 'Si el trace muestra Failed por transporte interno o el remitente está bloqueado por política del tenant (listas/reglas de seguridad): escalar a M365/security con el MessageTraceId y el NDR.',
    english_customer_response_template: 'Hi {{USERNAME}}, we investigated the message your sender mentioned. First we checked your Junk folder, the "Other" view and your inbox rules; the message was not there. We then traced the message in the company mail system and found it had been placed in quarantine as suspected spam. We reviewed it, confirmed it was a false positive, released it to your inbox, and reported it so future messages from this sender are not blocked. Please check your inbox now for the released message. If you ever expect an email that never arrives, the fastest details you can give us are the exact sender address and the time it was sent. Reference: ticket {{TICKET_ID}}.',
    english_technical_explanation: 'Missing inbound message for {{USERNAME}} on tenant {{TENANT}} reported at {{TIMESTAMP}}. Local classification ruled out first (Junk, Focused Inbox Other view, client rules), followed by server rules and forwarding (none present, no compromise indicators). The tenant quarantine search located the message from the exact sender, classified as spam. The message trace (Get-MessageTrace with recipient and date range) showed the event as Quarantined; Get-MessageTraceDetail documented the filter decision. Remediation: message released from quarantine as a false positive and the sender allow-listed per policy. Mailbox quota verified with Get-MailboxStatistics (below limit). Verification: a test message from the sender arrived in the inbox and the trace shows Delivered. No transport failure, so no M365/security escalation.',
    keywords: ['correos', 'mail flow', 'message trace', 'quarantine', 'cuarentena', 'junk', 'spam', 'reglas', 'transport rules', 'ndr', 'get-messagetrace', 'exchange', 'focused inbox'],
