    english_technical_explanation: 'BitLocker recovery prompt at boot on {{HOSTNAME}} at {{TIMESTAMP}} after a BIOS update. Key ID (8 hex digits) read from the BitLocker screen; the 48-digit recovery key was retrieved from Entra (aka.ms/aadrecoverykey) by key ID match, entered at the prompt, and the system booted. Root cause documented: the BIOS update cleared TPM measurements, triggering recovery (get-tpm shows TpmReady True and Secure Boot active). Protector state verified with manage-bde -status and manage-bde -protectors -get (Protection On, TPM and RecoveryPassword protectors present). Because the key was exposed during support, it was rotated and re-escrowed in Intune. Verification: two clean reboots without the recovery prompt and the new key escrowed. The key value itself was not stored in the ticket.',
